A||||5||kiteman||Headlight Problems - Need Help||||5||
Z||000000||kiteman||11-28-2001||09:56 PM||||Both headlights won't retract.  The passenger's side is up about half way.  The passenger's side motor kept running until I disconnected the relay. Also, my instrument panel and parking lights now don't work.  All fuses are OK.<P>This all started today when I turned the car on after I filled up at a gas station.  It was raining pretty hard.  Before that, everything was OK.<P>I could use some help in diagnosing the problem(s). The passenger's side motor was rebuilt a few months ago.  Do I need to try again, or is this another problem?||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||11-28-2001||11:02 PM||||Please don't take this as an insult, but please re-check the taillight fuse.  When it's "both headlights won't go down," that's what I look at first.  If the fuse is okay, then inspect the connectors in front compartment - C100 (the great big square one near brake M/C), and the connector to the isolation relay.<P>For the "motor doesn't stop running,"  I suspect something in the motors - HTS or stripped gear (I know you said you already rebuilt it, and I don't mean to imply you did anything wrong).  The above are <B>just</B> suggestions where to start looking  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||kiteman||11-29-2001||09:54 AM||||Appreciate the help, and I sure don't take any suggestions in a negative way.  As it turns out, you were right on target.  I took out the wrong 20a fuse yesterday as I was running through the diagnostics.  When I pulled the taillight fuse, sure enough, it was blown.  Replaced it and the drivers side motor now works.<P>The passengers side gear is obviously stripped.  I ordered a new one from Rodney Dickman's site last night.<P>Thanks again for the help.||||reg||10
Z||000003||StuGood||11-29-2001||05:05 PM||||That's great to hear!  The only thing is, now one might wonder what made the taillight fuse blow in the first place, eh?<P>If it's an intermittent short, it may happen again.  Time to start snooping around, for chafing of the wires going to the taillights, front parking lights, etc.  Hopefully, you will find something, and you'll have the "Aha!!"  experience.  Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">     ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Monkeyman||11-29-2001||08:14 PM||||A quick word of advice when changing the gear.  Make damn sure you keep the magnet thing (round/oval shaped metal thing surrounding the coiled wire) oriented correctly when you reinstall it (I found it easier to completely gut the casings and wash them to get the remaining green stuff out).  If you get it 180* off, your headlight will go up but not come back down.  I just found this out tonight.  (Thanx again, Rodrv6.)||||reg||1
Z||000005||kiteman||11-30-2001||01:40 PM||||Thanks for the tip on the magnet.  I'll make sure I get the right orientation when I do the rebuild.  I didn't pay attention to it the last time, and it worked.  Probably pure dumb luck.<P>I'll look around for the chafed insulation.  The fact that it happened when it was raining hard makes me think this may be a problem.<P>I appreciate all the help.||||reg||10
